%2Ficons%2Ffacebook.png&w=96&q=75)\n- ![Twitter](https://www.adityabirla.com/_next/image/?url=%2Ficons%2Fx.png&w=96&q=75)\n- ![Linkedin](https://www.adityabirla.com/_next/image/?url=%2Ficons%2Flinkedin.png&w=96&q=75)\n- ![WhatsApp](https://www.adityabirla.com/_next/image/?url=%2Ficons%2Fwhatsapp.png&w=96&q=75)\n- ![Copy Link](https://www.adityabirla.com/_next/image/?url=%2Ficons%2Fcopy-link.png&w=96&q=75)\n\nCopy\n\n\n[Home](https://www.adityabirla.com/)\u276f[Media](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/)\u276f[Press Releases](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/)\u276fAditya Birla Capital Q1 FY26 financial results: Consolidated PAT and Revenues up 10%\n\n- Consolidated Revenue1: Rs. 11,333 crore (\u219110% y-o-y)\n- Consolidated profit after tax1: Rs. 835 crore (\u219110% y-o-y)\n- Total lending portfolio: Rs. 1,65,832 crore (\u2191 30% y-o-y and 5% q-o-q)\n- Portfolio quality holds strong amidst uncertain environment\n- Mutual fund quarterly average AUM: Rs. 4,03,479 crore (\u2191 14% y-o-y)\n- Life insurance individual first year premium: Rs. 795 crore (\u2191 23% y-o-y)\n- Health insurance gross written premium: Rs. 1,357 crore (\u2191 30% y-o-y)\n- Udyog Plus, B2B platform for MSMEs reached \u00a03,658 crore AUM\n- ABCD, omnichannel D2C platform with ~ 6.4 mn customer acquisitions till date\n\n[Aditya Birla Capital Limited](https://www.adityabirla.com/businesses/companies/aditya-birla-capital-limited-abcl/) (\u201cThe Company\u201d) announced its unaudited financial results for the quarter ended June 30, 2025.\n\nThe consolidated revenue1 grew by 10% year-on-year to Rs. 11,333 crore. The consolidated operating profit grew by 13% year-on-year to Rs. 1,406 crore. The consolidated profit after tax grew by 10% year-on-year to Rs. 835 crore. The overall lending portfolio (NBFC and HFC) grew by 30% year-on-year and 5% sequentially to Rs. 1,65,832 crore as on June 30, 2025. The total AUM (AMC, life insurance and health insurance) grew by 20% year-on-year to Rs. 5,53,504 crore as on June 30, 2025. The life insurance individual first year premium grew by 23% year-on-year to Rs. 795 crore and health insurance gross written premium grew by 30% year-on-year to Rs. 1,357 crore.\n\nThe Company\u2019s D2C platform, ABCD offers a comprehensive portfolio of more than 25 products and services such as payments, loans, insurance, and investments. It helps customers to fulfil their financial needs and serves as an acquisition engine for the Company. The platform has witnessed a strong response with about 6.4 million customer acquisitions till date.\n\nThe comprehensive B2B platform for the MSME ecosystem, Udyog Plus, offers seamless, paperless digital journey for business loans, supply chain financing and a host of other value-added services. It has scaled up significantly with more than 2.4 million registrations and reached an AUM of Rs. 3,658 crore as of June 30, 2025.\n\nThe Company also continues to expand its pan-India network with 67 new branches added taking the total branch count across all businesses to 1,690 as of June 30, 2025. The branch expansion is targeted at driving penetration into tier 3 and tier 4 towns and new customer segments.\n\n### **Highlights of NBFC business**\n\n- Disbursements grew by 18% year-on-year to Rs. 15,851 crore\n- AUM grew by 22% year-on-year and 4% sequentially to Rs. 1,31,227 crore\n- Profit before tax grew by 11% year-on-year and 5% sequentially to Rs. 925 crore\n- Return on assets was 2.25%\n- Gross stage 2 and 3 ratio improved by 75 bps year-on-year and 8 bps sequentially to 3.70%\n\n### **Highlights of Housing Finance business**\n\n- Disbursements grew by 76% year-on-year to Rs. 5,404 crore\n- AUM grew by 70% year-on-year and 11% sequentially to Rs. 34,605 crore\n- Profit before tax grew by 82% year-on-year and 27% sequentially to Rs. 154 crore\n- Return on assets increased by 15 bps sequentially to 1.59%\n- Return on equity increased by 132 bps sequentially to 12.27%\n- Gross stage 2 and 3 ratio improved by 5 bps sequentially and 129 bps year-on-year to 1.34%\n\n### **Highlights of Asset Management business**\n\n- Mutual fund quarterly average assets under management grew by 14% year-on-year to Rs. 4,03,479 crore with equity mix at 44.7%\n- Equity QAAUM grew by 11% year-on-year to Rs. 1,80,184 crore\n- Individual monthly average assets under management grew by 10% year-on-year to Rs. 2,03,813 crore\n- Monthly systematic investment plan (SIP) flows grew by 4% year-on-year to Rs. 1,140 crore in June, 2025\n- Operating profit grew by 21% year-on-year to 254 crore\n\n### **Highlights of Life Insurance business**\n\n- Individual First Year Premium (FYP) grew by 23% year-on-year to Rs. 795 crore\n- Market share in individual FYP increased by 60 bps year-on-year to 5.1%\n- Renewal premium grew by 18% year-on-year to Rs. 1,978 crore\n- 13th month persistency: continued to be top quartile in industry at 87%\n- Net value of new business (VNB) margin increased by 109 bps to 7.5%\n- Absolute net VNB grew by 27% year-on-year to Rs. 66 core\n\n### **Highlights of Health Insurance business**\n\n- Gross written premium (GWP) grew by 30% year-on-year to Rs. 1,357 crore\n- Standalone health insurer (SAHI) market share increased by 200 bps year-on-year to 14.5%\n- Combined ratio improved to 111% (Q1 FY25: 112%)\n\n_1\\. Consolidated segment revenue and profit before tax; for Ind AS statutory reporting purpose Asset management, wellness business and health insurance are not consolidated and included under equity accounting._\n\nOther Available Locale - \\[\\]\n\nRelated Press Releases\n\n19 May, 2026\n\nAditya Birla Capital raises Rs. 4,000 crores of Equity Capital to Fund Growth\n\n![clock](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/clockGrey.svg)4 Minute Read\n\n[Click to Read More![default](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/link-maroon.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/aditya-birla-capital-raises-rs-4000-crores-of-equity-capital-to-fund-growth/)\n\n3 May, 2026\n\nAditya Birla Capital announces robust Q4 FY26 results\n\n![clock](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/clockGrey.svg)4 Minute Read\n\n[Click to Read More![default](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/link-maroon.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/aditya-birla-capital-announces-robust-q4-fy26-results/)\n\n3 February, 2026\n\nAditya Birla Capital posts strong Q3 FY26 results\n\n![clock](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/clockGrey.svg)4 Minute Read\n\n[Click to Read More![default](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/link-maroon.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/aditya-birla-capital-posts-strong-q3-fy26-results/)\n\n29 October, 2025\n\nAditya Birla Capital Q2 FY26 Financial Results \\| Consol. PAT rises 3% YoY to Rs 855 Crore\n\n![clock](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/clockGrey.svg)4 Minute Read\n\n[Click to Read More![default](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/link-maroon.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/aditya-birla-capital-q2-fy26-financial-results-consol-pat-rises-3-yoy-to-rs-855-crore/)\n\n[Load More![loadmore](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/link-loadmore-maroon.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/press-releases/aditya-birla-capital-q1-fy26-financial-results-consolidated-pat-and-revenues-up-10/#)\n\nFor Media Related Enquiries, Please Contact:\n\nMr. Sandeep Gurumurthi\n\nGroup Head, Communication & Brand\n\nAditya Birla Management Corporation Pvt. Ltd.\n\nCall: +91-22-6652-5000 / 2499-5000\n\nFax: +91-22-6652-5741 / 42\n\nMail: [sandeep.gurumurthi@adityabirla.com](mailto:sandeep.gurumurthi@adityabirla.com)\n\n![Dark Mode](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/moon.svg)[![Podcast](https://www.adityabirla.com/icons/podcast.svg)](https://www.adityabirla.com/media/podcasts/ \"Podcasts\")\n\n- [Contact Us](https://www.adityabirla.com/contact-us/)\n- [Careers](https://careers.adityabirla.com/)\n- [Privacy Notice](https://www.adityabirla.com/privacy-notice/)\n- [Aditya Birla Group Leadership Program