t \u20b915,851 crore (+18% YoY). Net Interest Income (NII) grew 9% YoY to \u20b91,859 crore, and PAT improved by 11% YoY to \u20b9689 crore. However, margins moderated to 5.97% (-25 bps YoY), largely due to lower yields. Housing finance, disbursements surged 76% YoY and AUM rose 70% YoY to \u20b934,605 crore. PAT for the segment jumped 80% YoY to \u20b9119 crore. Life insurance premium rose 23% and health GWP grew 30%.Combined ratio for the health segment improved to 111% (vs 112% YoY), reflecting improving operating metrics.\n\n**View:**\u00a0While the company posted strong topline and steady asset quality, softer margins and declining provision coverage remain key monitorable.\n\n**Impact:**\n\n## top 5 news\n\n#### [GrafTech Q2 Sales Up 8% YoY; Net Loss Narrows to $41M](https://www.icicidirect.com/research/equity/trending-news/graftech-q2-sales-up-8-yoy-net-loss-narrows-to-41m)\n\n27-Jul-2026 09:19\n\n#### [SAIL Q1FY27 PAT Jumps to \u20b91,644 Cr on Margin Growth](https://www.icicidirect.com/research/equity/trending-news/sail-q1fy27-pat-jumps-to-1-644-cr-on-margin-growth)\n\n27-Jul-2026 09:18\n\n#### [Maruti Suzuki launches Brezza Turbo Boosterjet at \u20b97.39 lakh with a 1.0L engine](https://www.icicidirect.com/research/equity/trending-news/maruti-suzuki-launches-brezza-turbo-boosterjet-at-739-lakh-with-a-10l-engine)\n\n27-Jul-2026 09:17\n\n#### [Laurus Labs Q1: Revenue up 29% to \u20b92,026 cr, EBITDA jumps to \u20b9638 cr, and PAT hits \u20b9362 cr](https://www.icicidirect.com/research/equity/trending-news/laurus-labs-q1-revenue-up-29-to-2-026-cr-ebitda-jumps-to-638-cr-and-pat-hits-362-cr)\n\n27-Jul-2026 09:16\n\n#### [Sakar Healthcare: Revenue up 38% to \u20b973Cr, PAT surges 120% to \u20b910.3Cr.](https://www.icicidirect.com/research/equity/trending-news/sakar-healthcare-revenue-up-38-to-73cr-pat-surges-120-to-103cr)\n\n27-Jul-2026 09:15\n\n### Explore more\n\n[IPO](https://www.icicidirect.com/ipo) [Mutual Funds](https://www.icicidirect.com/mutual-funds/mon